Output Naming Conventions
Converted SQL file
Use the source file base name and change the extension to .sql.

Example:

Scala_Code/Inv_Mbr_Enroll/InvprspMbrEnrollmentLoad.scala
→ SQL_Code/Inv_Mbr_Enroll/InvprspMbrEnrollmentLoad.sql
GenAISA config SQL files
Use:

genaisa_config_<app_name>_uat.sql
genaisa_config_<app_name>_prod.sql
Example:

genaisa_config_invprsp_uat.sql
genaisa_config_invprsp_prod.sql
Important Behaviors Enforced by the Prompt
The prompt is designed to enforce the following behaviors:

wrap scripts in EXECUTE IMMEDIATE $$...$$
use a single DECLARE section
use :variable syntax
use Jinja2 placeholders such as {{ targetTable }}
preserve the structure of TEMPLATE_snowflake_scripting.sql
create validation_counts
use transaction boundaries
preserve export/file naming logic
use explicit final target INSERT column lists
generate environment-specific config SQL when required
COPY INTO Path Convention
When the source job writes files to a Snowflake stage, the preferred generated pattern is:

@{{ snow_flake_stage }}/{{ s3_folder_path }}/{{ TIMESTAMP_FOLDER }}/<file_name_prefix>{{ TIMESTAMP_DATE }}
This keeps:

stage name separate from folder path
timestamp folder logic intact
filename prefix consistent with the source job
Environment-Specific GenAISA Rules
For config SQL generation:

UAT
Use:

USE SCHEMA U01_RAA.RAA_RAWZ;
PROD
Use:

USE SCHEMA P01_RAA.RAA_RAWZ;
SQL file path format
UAT:

s3://crln-raa-uat-codez-nogbd-phi-useast1/raa/genaisa/sql/<SUB_GROUP_NAME>/<SQL_FILE>
PROD:

s3://crln-raa-prod-codez-nogbd-phi-useast1/raa/genaisa/sql/<SUB_GROUP_NAME>/<SQL_FILE>
Recommended Review Checklist
Before accepting generated output, confirm that:

the correct module was converted
the SQL file is in the right SQL_Code/<module_name>/ folder
Author uses the expected domain ID
Co-Author is Devin, GPT-5.4 High Thinking
final INSERT statements use explicit target column lists
export path logic matches the source implementation
helper files were considered when generating Lambda or stitching config
fields not provided by the user were handled according to the prompt (NULL vs placeholder)
